h(2, id: "lists") { 7. Lists }

p {
    A list contains code{item} and code{task} children only. Zero items is a
    semantic error.
}

codeblock(lang: "text") {!
list {
  item { First }
  item { Second }
}

list(ordered: true) {
  item { Step one }
  item { Step two }
}
!}

p {
    code{ordered: true} emits code{<ol>}. Anything else, including omitting the
    attribute, emits code{<ul>}. code{start: N} sets the ordered-list start
    index. N must be 1 or greater. It is ignored on unordered lists.
}

codeblock(lang: "text") {!
list(ordered: true, start: 3) {
  item { Continues from 3 }
}
!}

h(3, id: "tasks") { 7.1 Tasks }

codeblock(lang: "text") {!
list {
  task(done: false) { Open work }
  task(done: true) { Finished work }
}
!}

p {
    code{done} is a boolean. Missing code{done} is treated as false. The
    checkbox is rendered disabled.
}

list {
    task(done: true) { Write the grammar down }
    task(done: false) { Add a new block type }
}

h(3, id: "nested-lists") { 7.2 Nested lists }

p {
    A list may appear inside an item. It must be the last child of that
    item.fn("item-nest")
}

codeblock(lang: "text") {!
list {
  item {
    Parent text
    list {
      item { Child }
      item { Other child }
    }
  }
  item { Sibling of the parent }
}
!}

list {
    item {
        Block types
        list {
            item { Prose: h, p, quote, callout }
            item { Structure: list, table, toc }
            item { Pass-through: raw, codeblock, math }
        }
    }
    item { Inline types: b, i, strike, code, m, link, fn }
}

list(ordered: true) {
    item { Parse }
    item { Analyze }
    item { Generate }
}

h(2, id: "quotes") { 8. Quotes }

p {
    A block quote. Body is prose and, optionally, one nested quote at the end.
    Optional attributes: code{cite} (URL) and code{author}.
}

codeblock(lang: "text") {!
quote(cite: "https://example.com", author: "Ada") {
  Outer line.
  quote {
    Inner line.
  }
}
!}

quote {
    A quote is a block, not an inline. Consecutive text inside it becomes one
    paragraph in HTML.

    quote {
        The inner quote closes the outer body. Do not put text after it.
    }
}
